<title>INDONESIA: Duta Pertiwi soars on rights issue talk.</title>
<headline>Duta Pertiwi soars on rights issue talk.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian formaldehyde and adhesive maker PT Duta Pertiwi soared in late trading on Monday on market talk of a possible rights issue, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;I heard the company is going to propose a rights issue. It really boosted sentiment,&quot; a broker with a London-based brokerage said.</p>
<p>The counter rose about 27 percent, or 500 rupiah, to 2,325 on a volume of about 7.5 million shares.</p>
<p>Company officials were not available for comment.</p>
</text>
